# Photographs for the Scan eval (eval/README.md): megabytes each, never
# diffed, and a growing set. Their expectations sit beside them as JSON and
# stay plain text, so a review reads what changed without fetching a pointer.
#
# Nothing in CI fetches these: `actions/checkout` leaves LFS alone unless
# asked, and `eval/` is out of the Docker build context.
# Case classes rather than lowercase patterns: an iPhone exports IMG_0001.JPG,
# and on a case-sensitive filesystem a lowercase pattern matches none of it —
# the photograph then enters history as a blob no later fix removes. This
# clone's `core.ignorecase` hides that, which is why it is spelled out.
eval/images/**/*.[jJ][pP][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
eval/images/**/*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
eval/images/**/*.[pP][nN][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
eval/images/**/*.[hH][eE][iI][cC] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
